{"alignments":[],"candidates":[{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"1,2,3","reason":"Adding all equations gives 2(x+y+z)=12. Thus x=6-5=1, y=6-4=2, and z=6-3=3.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_093_q1","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"5,4,3","reason":"Since x=y+1 and z=y-1, the total becomes 3y=12. Therefore y=4, x=5, and z=3.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_093_q3","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"2,3,1","reason":"Adding the first two equations gives 3x=6. Subtracting the second from the third gives 2y=6. Thus x=2, y=3, and z=1.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_093_q4","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"3,1,2","reason":"Adding gives x+y+z=6. Comparing twice this relation with the first two equations gives x-z=1 and y-z=-1, so z=2, x=3, and y=1.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_093_q5","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E (92)","reason":"A new dimension cannot use the same brick side as the corresponding old dimension: neither 2t = 3t + 1 nor 7t = 3t + 1 has a positive integer solution. Thus, up to relabeling, 2b = 3a + 1, 2c = 3b + 1, and 7a = 3c + 1. Solving gives (a,b,c) = (19,29,44), which are pairwise coprime. Their sum is 92.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2024_AMC_10B_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p160","cnm_p158","cnm_042","cnm_035"],"id":"match-edges-and-substitute","label":"Match the block edges, then substitute","methodDirectNodeIds":{"match-edges-and-substitute":["cnm_093","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_089"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_089","cnm_p160","cnm_p158","cnm_042","cnm_035"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 338","reason":"There are 8^3 - 7·6·5 = 302 systems with a zero or repeated coefficient row; each admits a nonzero solution. For distinct nonzero rows, elimination leaves exactly six unordered eligible triples: the patterns {x, y, x+y} = 0 and {x, y+z, x+y+z} = 0, each with three distinct variable relabelings. Their 3! equation orders contribute 36 more systems, giving 302 + 36 = 338.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2022_AMC_10B_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"classify-equation-triples","label":"Separate repeated and distinct equations","methodDirectNodeIds":{"classify-equation-triples":["cnm_h232","cnm_093","cnm_h234","cnm_h010"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h232","cnm_093","cnm_h234","cnm_h010"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"2,3,6","reason":"From x=2 and x+y=5, y=3. Then y+z=9 gives z=6, satisfying all three equations.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_093_q2","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 720","reason":"The equations give ab+ac = 152, ab+bc = 162, and ac+bc = 170. Their sum yields ab+bc+ca = 242, so ab = 72, bc = 90, and ca = 80. Hence abc = √(72×90×80) = 720, using positivity.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2002_AMC_12B_Q19","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_145","cnm_074"],"id":"solve-for-pair-products","label":"Treat the pair products as unknowns","methodDirectNodeIds":{"solve-for-pair-products":["cnm_093","cnm_143","cnm_075"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093","cnm_143","cnm_075","cnm_145","cnm_074"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":0,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D (7)","reason":"The total of the three numbers is (12 + 17 + 19)/2 = 24. Subtracting the pair sums gives 12, 7, and 5, whose middle number is 7.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2012_AMC_12A_Q06","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"linear-elimination","label":"Eliminate three unknowns","methodDirectNodeIds":{"linear-elimination":["cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, -61","reason":"The missing cubic term makes the fourth root -6. The pairwise-product sum is a=-25, and the root product is c=-36. Thus a+c=-61.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1966_AMC_12_Q30","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"id":"substitute-three-roots","label":"Solve for the coefficients directly","nodeIds":["cnm_029","cnm_093"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_039","cnm_032","cnm_021","cnm_090"],"id":"solution:substitute-three-roots:20b62270a2bb","label":"Substitute the known roots","methodDirectNodeIds":{"substitute-three-roots":["cnm_029","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_029","cnm_093","cnm_039","cnm_032","cnm_021","cnm_090"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 1.2 hours","reason":"The total rate is 1 tank/hour. Thus B = 1 - 2/3 = 1/3 and A = 1 - 1/2 = 1/2. Their combined rate is 5/6, so the time is 6/5 = 1.2 hours.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1973_AMC_12_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"three-rate-system","label":"Solve a three-rate system","methodDirectNodeIds":{"three-rate-system":["cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 7","reason":"The three numbers total (12+17+19)/2 = 24. Subtracting each pair sum from 24 gives 12, 7, and 5, so the middle number is 7.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2012_AMC_10A_Q08","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"linear-elimination","label":"Eliminate three unknowns","methodDirectNodeIds":{"linear-elimination":["cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 36.8","reason":"If the set has n elements, then 72=(40-32)(n-1), so n=10. The eight middle elements total 35*8=280, and the least is 32*9-280=8. The full total is 40*9+8=368, giving mean 36.8.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2021_AMC_10B_Q19","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"size-and-extremes-system","label":"Solve for the size and extremes together","methodDirectNodeIds":{"size-and-extremes-system":["cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: 75","reason":"Writing the numbers as a, b, c gives a+c=2b. Adding the given equations yields a+2b+c=100, so 4b=100 and a+b+c=3b=75.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2026_AMC_8_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"three-variable-system","label":"Solve a linear system","methodDirectNodeIds":{"three-variable-system":["cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"1, -2, -3","reason":"Write y=a(x+1)(x-3). The point (0,-3) gives -3=-3a, so y=x²-2x-3.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_233_q1","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"id":"coefficient-system","label":"Substitute the three points","nodeIds":["cnm_093"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"solution:coefficient-system:1ab1b5d12fc2","label":"Substitute the three points","methodDirectNodeIds":{"coefficient-system":["cnm_233","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_233","cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E: x=2abc/(ac+bc-ab)","reason":"Taking reciprocals gives 1/a=1/x+1/y, 1/b=1/x+1/z, and 1/c=1/y+1/z. Therefore 2/x=1/a+1/b-1/c=(ac+bc-ab)/(abc), yielding the stated expression.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":["All original fractions must be defined. For an existing solution, ac+bc-ab is also nonzero.","All original denominators must be nonzero; the displayed formula is asserted for parameter triples admitting an original solution."],"questionId":"1951_AMC_12_Q44","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"id":"linearize-reciprocals","label":"Linearize using reciprocals","nodeIds":["cnm_016","cnm_093"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_156","cnm_161","cnm_040"],"id":"solution:linearize-reciprocals:ae38fbdcfe4d","label":"Take reciprocals to obtain linear relations","methodDirectNodeIds":{"linearize-reciprocals":["cnm_165","cnm_016","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_165","cnm_016","cnm_093","cnm_156","cnm_161","cnm_040"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 26 cents","reason":"Working backward from (16,16,16) gives balances (8,8,32) before C's turn, then (4,28,16) before B's turn, and finally (26,14,8) initially. Thus A starts with 26 cents.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1963_AMC_12_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"model-three-balances","label":"Model three initial balances","methodDirectNodeIds":{"model-three-balances":["cnm_027","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_027","cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E: 12","reason":"Write y = a(x-4)^2 + 2. Substituting (2,0) gives a = -1/2, so y = -(1/2)x^2 + 4x - 6 and abc = 12.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1986_AMC_12_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"solve-general-coefficients","label":"General-form coefficients","methodDirectNodeIds":{"solve-general-coefficients":["cnm_232","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_232","cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, 39","reason":"Let p,q,r be the corner-hitting probabilities from the center, an axial neighbor, and a diagonal neighbor. First-step equations are 8p=4q+4r, 8q=p+2q+2r, and 8r=1+p+2q. They give p=4/35, so m+n=39. Absorption is almost sure because three consecutive northward moves guarantee a boundary hit from any interior position.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2017_AMC_12A_Q22","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"three-state-first-step","label":"Group positions by symmetry","methodDirectNodeIds":{"three-state-first-step":["math:recursive-counting-probability","cnm_h246","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["math:recursive-counting-probability","cnm_h246","cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 10","reason":"Every root r satisfies r³=5r²-8r+13. Multiplying by r^(k-2) and summing over the roots gives s_(k+1)=5s_k-8s_(k-1)+13s_(k-2). Thus (a,b,c)=(5,-8,13), and a+b+c=10.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2019_AMC_12A_Q17","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"sum-root-equations","label":"Use the equation each root satisfies","methodDirectNodeIds":{"sum-root-equations":["math:polynomial-roots-coefficients","cnm_h200","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["math:polynomial-roots-coefficients","cnm_h200","cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 29","reason":"Write F(i,j)=A+B(i-1)+C(j-1)+D(i-1)(j-1), as required by the row and column progressions. The four specified entries force (A,B,C,D)=(12,0,17,-5). Therefore F(1,2)=12+17=29.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2024_AMC_12A_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"bilinear-array-parameters","label":"Parameterize entries using arithmetic terms","methodDirectNodeIds":{"bilinear-array-parameters":["cnm_h202","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h202","cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A (28 years old)","reason":"For s students, t teachers, and Ash's age a, the averages give a=2s+14 and a=52−3t. Together with s+t=15, these yield s=7, t=8, and a=28.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2025_AMC_12A_Q03","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"team-count-linear-system","label":"Team counts and age system","methodDirectNodeIds":{"team-count-linear-system":["cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"-2, -4, 0","reason":"Write y=a(x+1)²+2. Substituting (1,-6) gives a=-2, so y=-2x²-4x.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_233_q3","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"general-coefficients","label":"Use general-form constraints","methodDirectNodeIds":{"general-coefficients":["cnm_232","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_232","cnm_093"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 3 days","reason":"The pair rates are a+b=1/2, b+c=1/4, and a+c=5/12. Hence 2a=1/2+5/12-1/4=2/3, so a=1/3 job per day and A needs 3 days.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1954_AMC_12_Q30","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_016","cnm_p174"],"id":"combine_work_rates","label":"Add and subtract work rates","methodDirectNodeIds":{"combine_work_rates":["cnm_046","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_046","cnm_093","cnm_016","cnm_p174"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, k=3","reason":"Since c=-a-b, f(7)=6(8a+b)=54 and f(8)=7(9a+b)=77. Thus a=2, b=-7, c=5. Consequently f(100)=19305, which lies strictly between 15000 and 20000, so k=3.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2011_AMC_12A_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"coefficient-elimination","label":"Eliminate coefficients using the evaluations","methodDirectNodeIds":{"coefficient-elimination":["cnm_093","cnm_090"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093","cnm_090"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"5","reason":"Set a = 2k, b = 3k, c = 5k. Then 2a + 3b - c = (4 + 9 - 5)k = 8k = 20, so k = 5/2 and a = 5. Substituting b = 3a/2 and c = 5a/2 also gives 4a = 20.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_268_q4","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"direct-substitution","label":"Substitute in terms of a","methodDirectNodeIds":{"direct-substitution":["cnm_093","cnm_089","cnm_044"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_093","cnm_089","cnm_044"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B ({4,5,7})","reason":"For sorted face diagonals u,v,w, one squared edge is (u^2+v^2-w^2)/2, so u^2+v^2 must exceed w^2. Only {4,5,7} fails: 16+25<49. Each other listed set gives three positive squared edges.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1993_AMC_12_Q29","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p160","cnm_186","cnm_074"],"id":"recover-squared-edges","label":"Recover the squared edge lengths","methodDirectNodeIds":{"recover-squared-edges":["cnm_174","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_174","cnm_093","cnm_p160","cnm_186","cnm_074"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E (14π)","reason":"Writing the radii at A, B, C as x, y, z gives x+y=3, x+z=4, and y+z=5. Thus x=1, y=2, z=3, and the total area is π(1²+2²+3²)=14π.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2006_AMC_12A_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p188","cnm_040"],"id":"tangent_radius_sums","label":"Use the sums of tangent radii","methodDirectNodeIds":{"tangent_radius_sums":["cnm_h181","cnm_093","cnm_p192"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h181","cnm_093","cnm_p192","cnm_p188","cnm_040"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: √95","reason":"Assign AB = 5, AC = 7, and BC = 6, and let OA = x, OB = y, OC = z. Then x^2 + y^2 = 25, x^2 + z^2 = 49, and y^2 + z^2 = 36, giving x^2 = 19, y^2 = 6, z^2 = 30. The volume is xyz/6 = √(19 × 6 × 30)/6 = √95.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2008_AMC_12A_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h151","cnm_p148","cnm_074"],"id":"perpendicular-edge-squares","label":"Find the three edges from the origin","methodDirectNodeIds":{"perpendicular-edge-squares":["cnm_174","cnm_h111","cnm_093"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_174","cnm_h111","cnm_093","cnm_h151","cnm_p148","cnm_074"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":6,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: 22","reason":"Degrees give 3 deg(Q)=6, so deg(Q)=2. Divisibility requires Q(1),Q(2),Q(3)∈{1,2,3}. The 27 value triples determine unique polynomials of degree at most two. Exclude three constant triples and (1,2,3),(3,2,1), leaving 22.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2005_AMC_12A_Q24","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_032","cnm_029","cnm_093"],"id":"values-determine-quadratic","label":"Count the possible values at the three roots","methodDirectNodeIds":{"values-determine-quadratic":["math:polynomial-remainder-factor","math:bijective-counting","cnm_233","cnm_h231"]},"nodeIds":["math:polynomial-remainder-factor","math:bijective-counting","cnm_233","cnm_h231","cnm_032","cnm_029","cnm_093"]}]}],"layer":"ailleo","meaning":"Reviewed content-bound concept practice; no claim of complete source-standard coverage or learner mastery.","nextOffset":null,"nodeId":"cnm_093","status":"mapped","total":30}
